---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
    <section class="privacy-section">
        <section id="gdpr-information">
            <h2>GDPR Information</h2>

            <p>
                FossilGeo is designed to collect as little personal data as possible. Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), FossilGeo acts as a
                “data controller” for any personal information you choose to provide.
            </p>

            <h3>What Personal Data FossilGeo Processes</h3>
            <p>FossilGeo only processes the following categories of personal data:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Technical data handled automatically</strong><br />
                    This includes browser type, device type, approximate region, and request metadata required to operate the site securely and reliably. This information
                    is processed automatically by hosting and infrastructure services and is not used to identify individual users.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Email communications</strong><br />
                    If you contact FossilGeo by email, your email address, message content, and related metadata are stored solely for the purpose of responding
                    to your enquiry and maintaining a support inbox.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                FossilGeo does <strong>not</strong> create user accounts, does <strong>not</strong> track users across sites, and does <strong>not</strong> build
                behavioural profiles.
            </p>

            <h3>Legal Basis for Processing</h3>
            <p>FossilGeo processes personal data under the following GDPR legal bases:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Legitimate Interests (Article 6(1)(f))</strong><br />
                    For technical data required to operate, secure, and maintain the website.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Consent (Article 6(1)(a))</strong><br />
                    When you choose to send an email to FossilGeo, you consent to the processing of the information contained in that message.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>How Long Data Is Kept</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Technical data is retained only temporarily as part of normal hosting logs.</li>
                <li>Email correspondence is kept only as long as necessary to manage support and communication, after which it may be archived or deleted.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Data Sharing</h3>
            <p>
                FossilGeo does not sell personal data and does not share it for advertising or marketing. Technical data may pass through hosting or
                infrastructure providers (e.g., Netlify) solely for operational purposes.
            </p>

            <h3>Your GDPR Rights</h3>
            <p>Under GDPR, you have the right to:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Access the personal data FossilGeo holds about you</li>
                <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
                <li>Request deletion of your personal data</li>
                <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
                <li>Request restriction of processing</li>
                <li>Request a copy of your data in a portable format</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                To exercise any of these rights, contact:
                <a href="mailto:privacy@fossilgeo.uk">privacy@fossilgeo.uk</a>
            </p>

            <h3>International Data Transfers</h3>
            <p>
                FossilGeo may use hosting or email services located outside the UK/EU. When this occurs, reasonable steps are taken to ensure appropriate
                safeguards are in place, such as standard contractual clauses or equivalent protections.
            </p>

            <h3>Security</h3>
            <p>
                Reasonable technical and organisational measures are used to protect personal data. However, no online service can guarantee perfect security.
            </p>

            <h3>Updates</h3>
            <p>This GDPR section may be updated if FossilGeo’s features or data handling practices change.</p>
        </section>

        <p>This page may be updated from time to time if the site changes.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2.5 italic">&copy; 2026 FossilGeo. All rights reserved.</p>
    </section>
</Layout>
